From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 40/59] fakeip: a store that answers from memory and saves in
 the background

TableStore: the whole map in memory, saved to the cache file in the background, new names answered
while the file cannot be written, Peek tells an address without giving one. The transport makes it
in place of upstream's Store; upstream's store and memory storage stay as they are.

Made of these commits of the earlier series (branch archive/r25-1.14-commits):
  4021c908c dns/fakeip: answer from memory, save to the cache file in the background
  e4b0cb97b dns/fakeip: answer new names from memory while the cache file cannot be written
  b7f1fec4c dns/fakeip: tell the loop to stop before the store refuses saves
  11e6760c0 fakeip: Peek tells the address of a domain without giving it one
  448f5ebd0 fakeip: the store of the fork as TableStore, upstream's store and memory storage as upstream has them

